# Build context excludes — the Dockerfiles run a fresh `pnpm install` + build,
# so host artifacts are never needed and only slow the context upload.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
**/.turbo
coverage
.coredoc-ci
.r2-local

# Local coredoc runtime data — never COPYied by any Dockerfile. Excluding it
# keeps the build context small (coredoc.db alone is ~400MB, coredoc-output ~200MB),
# so every server/CLI image build/deploy uploads a lean context.
coredoc.db*
coredoc-output
coredoc-parsers
coredoc-sessions
